<title>THAILAND: REFERENCE RATE FIRMS TO 31.517-BANK OF THAILAND.</title>
<headline>REFERENCE RATE FIRMS TO 31.517-BANK OF THAILAND.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand on Friday said the weighted average interbank exchange rate was 31.517 per dollar against 31.618 on Thursday.</p>
<p>The reference rate is the average rate traded the previous day. It has been announced daily by the central bank since the July 2 managed flotation of the baht.</p>
<p>The baht was quoted at 31.05/31.35 to the dollar onshore and 30.70/30.80 in offshore markets early.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
